From 7c1cd5d0bd896fa09b284da84787fd27d97d8041 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:56:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Torus: observe the exact Lean release and clean
 dependencies after the last Lean run

replay.sh records `lean --version` and every installed dependency as
`<name> <HEAD> <clean|dirty>` before the first Lean execution (toolchain.log,
packages.log) and again after the last one (toolchain-final.log,
packages-final.log); git results are taken by plain assignment so a git
failure aborts under set -e. check.py finish requires both toolchain lines to
match the pinned release and be byte-identical, both package observations to
list exactly the manifest HEADs with clean worktrees, and records the final
observation in the receipt. EVIDENCE_FILES 72 -> 74.

Does not establish: that nothing changed between the two observations, any
alignment, review or acceptance; no claim, premise or label moves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cz7WZybv8znP64SpPj6sWY
